  <HOMEWORK title="PLL Bring-Up 6: Final sign-off" prompt="Every step so far is corrected and the stress test is behind it. With a clean reference restored, run the final sign-off the way a real bring-up lab would and confirm this synthesizer is ready: locked, on frequency, and settled - not just technically running."
            hint="Check all three together: the lock indicator, the output frequency against reference x N, and the instantaneous phase error once settled - not just whichever one looks best on its own."
            explanation="With every earlier fault corrected and a clean reference restored, the synthesizer locks cleanly, settles without the ringing Bring-Up 4 showed, and the output frequency lands on reference x N to within a small fraction of a percent - genuinely ready, not just technically running. This is the real final-sign-off habit this whole plan has been building toward: confirm the lock indicator, the actual output frequency, and the settled phase error together, the same &quot;don't trust a single number alone&quot; discipline Bring-Up 2 and Bring-Up 5 each already needed for their own reasons."/>
